  "summary": "I design smoothly operating user interfaces, remove and repair software bottlenecks, and upgrade your legacy systems to make users actually enjoy using your software! The web was meant to make life more convenient, not more infuriating. Broken or just plain ancient software causes unnecessary frustration to users and, as a result, makes them leave forever. This causes insane pressure for small teams of developers or folks who bought software and never upgraded it, but that's exactly the pressure I specialize in relieving.\n\nFor those looking for my technical qualifications, I am highly skilled in developing applications using Rest APIs in .NET and a frontend in Angular, or MVC / Razor if needed. Currently, i am learning Playwright to integrate automated user testing into my work. Contrary to popular sentiment, I actually favor JavaScript over all other languages. Aside from these, I also am experienced in T-SQL.",
